    "code": "# Python3 program to find number\n# of rotations in a sorted and\n# rotated array.\n \n# Returns count of rotations for\n# an array which is first sorted\n# in ascending order, then rotated\ndef countRotations(arr, n):\n \n    # We basically find index\n    # of minimum element\n    min = arr[0]\n    min_index = 0\n    for i in range(0, n):\n     \n        if (min > arr[i]):\n         \n            min = arr[i]\n            min_index = i\n         \n    return min_index;\n \n \n# Driver code\narr = [15, 18, 2, 3, 6, 12]\nn = len(arr)\nprint(countRotations(arr, n))\n \n# This code is contributed by Smitha Dinesh Semwal",
